cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Foothold: learn Python by watching your code run"
message: "If you use Foothold in teaching or research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Foothold contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jbtk-cell/foothold"
url: "https://jbtk-cell.github.io/foothold/"
abstract: >-
  A free, open source introductory Python course that runs entirely in the
  browser. It grades every exercise by executing it against real tests in
  CPython compiled to WebAssembly, and includes a step-through debugger inside
  each exercise so a learner can replay their own program a line at a time and
  watch the variables change.
keywords:
  - python
  - computer science education
  - programming education
  - introductory programming
  - webassembly
  - open educational resources
license: MIT
